# Title: Alarm Cascade
# Summary: A scalable chain of local alarm-response modules where each site can trigger the next site downstream.
# Benchmark Family: alarm_cascade
# Alarm_1: The alarm activates at site 1.
# Alarm_2: The alarm activates at site 2.
# Alarm_3: The alarm activates at site 3.
# Alarm_4: The alarm activates at site 4.
# Alarm_5: The alarm activates at site 5.
# Alarm_6: The alarm activates at site 6.
# Alarm_7: The alarm activates at site 7.
# Alarm_8: The alarm activates at site 8.
# Call_1: A local report call is made from site 1.
# Call_2: A local report call is made from site 2.
# Call_3: A local report call is made from site 3.
# Call_4: A local report call is made from site 4.
# Call_5: A local report call is made from site 5.
# Call_6: A local report call is made from site 6.
# Call_7: A local report call is made from site 7.
# Call_8: A local report call is made from site 8.
# Concern_1: Concern spreads among responders at site 1.
# Concern_2: Concern spreads among responders at site 2.
# Concern_3: Concern spreads among responders at site 3.
# Concern_4: Concern spreads among responders at site 4.
# Concern_5: Concern spreads among responders at site 5.
# Concern_6: Concern spreads among responders at site 6.
# Concern_7: Concern spreads among responders at site 7.
# Concern_8: Concern spreads among responders at site 8.
# Sensor_1: A local sensor detects an issue at site 1.
# Sensor_2: A local sensor detects an issue at site 2.
# Sensor_3: A local sensor detects an issue at site 3.
# Sensor_4: A local sensor detects an issue at site 4.
# Sensor_5: A local sensor detects an issue at site 5.
# Sensor_6: A local sensor detects an issue at site 6.
# Sensor_7: A local sensor detects an issue at site 7.
# Sensor_8: A local sensor detects an issue at site 8.

